============================================================
THE PUNCHLINE
============================================================

Every natural number n has a GOLDEN SHADOW:
  f_n = (n-2+sqrt(n^2+4))/2

  1. f_n has CF [n-2; n, n, n, ...] (periodic, partial quotient n)
  2. f_n satisfies f^2 - (n-2)f - n = 0 (golden-type equation)
  3. f_n maps to the Cayley address: x = (f^2+f-1)/(f^2+3f+1) = x_n
  4. The map is algebraic: quadratic irrational -> rational

The continued fraction [n-2; n, n, n, ...] is the SIMPLEST
periodic CF with partial quotient n. It is the 'n-metallic mean.'

The Cayley address x_n = (n-1)/(n+1) is the RATIONAL SHADOW
of the quadratic irrational f_n.

NUMBERS HAVE TWO FACES:
  Rational face: x_n = (n-1)/(n+1) on [0,1) (Cayley address)
  Irrational face: f_n = [n-2; n,n,n,...] (golden shadow)
  Both encode the same number n.
  The Cayley transform MEDIATES between them.
